# tools: the commands the tooling machine provides to a host that lacks them,
# one per line. provision.sh installs them and refuses a machine on which one
# is not found. The first group are the commands only Linux has among the
# platforms of tools/setup/prereqs: user namespaces, network tools and
# exfatprogs. The rest are what the GNU layer's build needs of its host
# (vendor/gnu/Readme.md, Building), the
# file-system checkers the suites run, and the checkers of the style cases,
# which tests/cases/host/style.sh runs here on a host that lacks the testing
# host's versions.
